# QA artifacts: contact sheets and extracted audio used to review video before
# delivery. Regenerate with _scripts/seedance-qa.mjs; never a deliverable.
_qa/
**/_qa/

# Batch 2 (2026-08-09) clean uncaptioned 1080p intermediates. The captioned
# *-captioned.mp4 files are the deliverable and ARE committed; these masters are
# 318 MB and would push the repo past 1.2 GB. Re-derive any of them by re-running
# the upscale from the committed 480p master (~$0.22 each):
#   node _scripts/seedance-generate.mjs --prompts seedance-prompts-b2.mjs \
#     --batch 2026-08-09-seedance-video-b2 --only <id>
*/2026-08-09-seedance-video-b2/*-1080p.mp4
*/2026-08-09-seedance-video-b2/*-1080p-fixed.mp4
*/2026-08-09-seedance-video-b2/*-1080p-trimmed.mp4

# Batch 10 (2026-08-18) clean uncaptioned 1080p intermediates, same call as
# batch 2 above: the *-captioned.mp4 files are the deliverable and ARE committed,
# these are another 119 MB of intermediate. Re-derive from the committed 720p
# master (~$0.14 each):
#   node _scripts/seedance-generate.mjs --prompts seedance-prompts-b10-bitpredict.mjs \
#     --batch 2026-08-18-viral-b10 --only <id>
#   node _scripts/seedance-endcard.mjs bitpredict/2026-08-13-reddit-b2/_work/endcard.png <clip>
# c8 and c15 additionally need their read-aloud stage direction muted before the
# end card is appended; the windows are recorded in the batch doc.
*/2026-08-18-viral-b10/*-1080p.mp4
*/2026-08-18-viral-b10/*-1080p-fixed.mp4
_review-*/

# Banner batches: raw/ is the un-composited render straight off fal and is a
# byte-for-byte duplicate of banners-nologo/, which IS committed. fonts/ are
# Google Fonts fetched at build time. Both are re-derivable from the prompts.
**/_work/raw/
**/_work/fonts/
# Generated review page: 2.9 MB of base64-inlined copies of banners/ that are
# already committed. Re-derive with _work/build-review-page.py.
**/_work/review-page.html

# Batch 9 (2026-08-13) TeamPredict video: the uncaptioned 1080p upscales and the
# v3 trim intermediate, 94 MB. The *-captioned.mp4 files are the deliverable and
# ARE committed, as are the cheap 720p masters. Re-derive an intermediate by
# re-running the upscale from the committed 720p master (~$0.11 each):
#   node _scripts/seedance-generate.mjs --prompts seedance-prompts-b9-teampredict.mjs \
#     --batch 2026-08-13-paid-launch-video --duration 15 --resolution 720p --only <id>
teampredict/2026-08-13-paid-launch-video/*-1080p.mp4
teampredict/2026-08-13-paid-launch-video/*-1080p-trimmed.mp4
# Generated status page: 372 KB of base64-inlined copies of thumbnails/ and the
# brand fonts, all already present. Re-derive with _work/build-status-page.py.
teampredict/2026-08-13-paid-launch-video/_work/status-page.html

# Batch 10 (2026-08-18) office skits: the uncaptioned 1080p upscales, 82 MB of
# intermediates. The *-captioned.mp4 files are the deliverable and ARE
# committed, as are the 720p generation masters. Re-derive an intermediate by
# re-running the upscale from the committed 720p master:
#   node _scripts/seedance-generate.mjs --prompts seedance-prompts-b10-teampredict-office.mjs \
#     --batch 2026-08-18-office-skits --duration 30 --resolution 720p --only <id>
teampredict/2026-08-18-office-skits/teampredict-w1-farewell-party-1080p.mp4
teampredict/2026-08-18-office-skits/teampredict-w2-exit-interview-1080p.mp4
teampredict/2026-08-18-office-skits/teampredict-w3-gone-quiet-1080p.mp4

# Heart-tug batch (2026-08-18): the uncaptioned pro-tier 1080p intermediates are
# 64 MB and re-derivable from the committed 720p masters for ~$1.08 each:
#   node _scripts/seedance-pro-upscale.mjs esacard/2026-08-18-heart-tug/<id>-720p.mp4
# The *-captioned.mp4 files are the deliverable and ARE committed.
esacard/2026-08-18-heart-tug/*-1080p.mp4
esacard/2026-08-18-heart-tug/*.mp3
# Batch 11 (2026-08-18) office skits round 2: same rule, uncaptioned 1080p
# intermediates stay out; captioned deliverables and 720p masters are committed.
teampredict/2026-08-18-office-skits-2/teampredict-w4-new-headshot-1080p.mp4
teampredict/2026-08-18-office-skits-2/teampredict-w5-conspiracy-board-1080p.mp4
teampredict/2026-08-18-office-skits-2/teampredict-w6-green-ring-1080p.mp4

# Batch 12 (2026-08-18) 1Lookup product videos. Same rule as batch 2: the
# *-captioned.mp4 deliverables (captions burned in, branded end card appended)
# ARE committed, along with the 720p Seedance masters they were built from.
# The uncaptioned/trimmed/muted 1080p intermediates are ~203 MB and are
# re-derivable by re-running the upscale and the trim/mute recorded in the
# batch README:
*/2026-08-18-product-videos/*-1080p.mp4
*/2026-08-18-product-videos/*-1080p-trimmed.mp4
*/2026-08-18-product-videos/*-1080p-fixed.mp4
# Superseded takes: the 720p masters of rejected rolls are kept as the record
# (they are what the README's re-roll comparison refers to); their 1080p
# upscales are not, at ~87 MB for takes that will never ship.
*/2026-08-18-product-videos/_rolls/*-1080p*.mp4

# Batch 13 (2026-08-19) end-card intermediates. Same call as batches 2 and 10
# above: the *-endcard-captioned.mp4 files are the deliverable and ARE committed;
# these are the same clip with only the card appended and no captions, another
# 119 MB of pure intermediate. Re-derive in seconds, no fal spend, with:
#   cp <clip>-1080p.mp4 <clip>-1080p-endcard.mp4
#   node _scripts/seedance-endcard.mjs \
#     1lookup/2026-08-13-youtube-google-ads/_work/endcard.png <clip>-1080p-endcard.mp4
*/2026-08-19-b13-product-videos/*-1080p-endcard.mp4

# Batch 13 rejected rolls: the 720p takes ARE committed, because they are the
# evidence for the README's two defect rows (a rotated frame and an inverted
# joke) and someone will want to see them. Their 1080p upscales are not, at
# ~30 MB for takes that will never ship.
*/2026-08-19-b13-product-videos/_rolls/*-1080p*.mp4

# ESA Card weird-animals batch (2026-08-19). The *-1080p.mp4 files are the deliverable
# and ARE committed; these are the intermediates and the discarded/backup takes:
#   _takes/take1/ holds the pre-re-roll masters of w1, w2, w4 and w5, kept only so a
#   worse second take can be discarded (batch 12: two of four re-rolls came back worse).
esacard/2026-08-19-weird-animals/_takes/

# Batch 2026-08-21 ("the turn"): _takes/take1/ holds t2's superseded take, whose
# audio garbled the brand phrase into "emotional support Weeder Red" on two
# independent transcription engines. Kept off the repo but on disk so the two
# takes can be compared, per the batch-12 rule that a re-roll is a coin flip.
esacard/2026-08-21-the-turn/_takes/
esacard/2026-08-19-weird-animals/*-take2-720p.mp4
esacard/2026-08-19-weird-animals/*.log
